// test/basic/let-stmt-errors.ta — NEGATIVE test: a block-scoped `let` that
// is NOT the first statement parses as a flat (let x val) form; its real
// type must still reach later statements, so a misuse after it is rejected
// (issue #90: the use unified the pre-registered tvar silently and the
// error site was lost).
// Expected: rejected by typecheck ("type error" in output, exit != 0),
// with BOTH error sites reported.
// expect: typecheck: 2 type error(s) found

fn main() {
  1 && true
  let x = true
  print(x + 1)
}
